Z||000009||Raydar||04-11-2001||02:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Taijiguy:<BR><B>A strobe light? *sigh* Is nothing sacred?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The original Fiero pace car actually had a strobe light (emergency light) in the back edge of the scoop. Used a 747 wing light lens for a cover. <BR>Not that it would look any less tacky on a street car. Might discourage those annoying tailgaters, though.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000010||MoneypitGT||04-11-2001||04:35 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://customdynamix.com/left.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://customdynamix.com/right.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://customdynamix.com/back.jpg"> <BR>I just took these picts, it is fiberglass and is not "bolt on." I bought it from a guy in Florida that makes them and sells them on Ebay. It is actually a nice piece. It can be made functional, you just have to cut out the lines that are already scored on there. I have also decided not to sell it, SORRY, but I will find the guys email address, I think I paid about $90 shipped.<BR>  Chris<P>------------------<BR><B>Check out my site at:</B>   <A HREF="http://www.customdynamix.com" TARGET=_blank>www.customdynamix.com</A> <BR>2 '87 GT Projects||||reg||1
