Z||000018||Oreif||04-11-2001||09:29 PM||||This is what your looking for:<P>The scoops are called, "Indy Fiero Scoop" or "SD4 street scoop" They can be bought thru IRM (1-800-367-8423) for $200 or the below website for $189.00.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.showcars-bodyparts.com/fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.showcars-bodyparts.com/fiero.html</A> <P>I got mine from IRM for $200 and made it functional.<BR> IRM says it's non-functional but you just cut out the opening in front and your decklid. The scoops come to fit 1984 coupes but have lines marked to fit 85-88 notchback or 86-88 fastback. (Trimming required for all except 1984) Mine is functional and does not use the hinge mount that IRM suggests. <P>The IRM one is the original DGP mold used on the Fiero race cars during the 80's IRM bought all the DGP molds for the IMSA/SD4 body kit's and scoops.<P>FOCOA sells a version but it's $350 for non-functional and $385 for functional. (the face is cut out and a screen is installed.)<BR>Prices are for non-members.<P><BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1986SE.jpg">     <P><BR>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 04-11-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000019||RNGCRSH||04-11-2001||09:56 PM||||You can get an original at a salvage yard off of a '79 mustang for about $20. Just let you fingers do the walking and you can save some bucks||||reg||1
